      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lottery-based systems are a great way to ensure equity, as they eliminate biases towards specific demographics. Prioritizing proximity to transit is a good idea, but it can inadvertently favor existing residents who already have access to better transportation options. Income-based lotteries, on the other hand, can be problematic if they're not carefully designed, as they may inadvertently favor low-income families who are already struggling to make ends meet.",
